// The figures you might meet out in the Territory (GDD §3.2; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 528): people who aren't the towns' and
// aren't creatures. The numbers (how often, where, how many blows) are in tuning/enemies.json; this file is only words,
// read by Game/FigureTalk. Text is written in sentence case and drawn in the HUD's capitals, in its letters (ASCII and
// àâçéèêëîïôùûü); keep a line under ~150 characters.
{
  // How close you come to talk, how far off the centre of your view, how far you walk off before the card closes, and how
  // far off you still hear him answer a blow. Typed at "typePerSecond", left up "lingerSeconds" once said.
  "reach": { "talk": 3.2, "lookDegrees": 22, "closeBeyond": 6, "hearBeyond": 30 },
  "typePerSecond": 40,
  "lingerSeconds": 6,

  // DAVE (the director, 8 Oct 2026: "His name is Dave (just Dave) and he's a wandering painter ... painting beautiful
  // landscapes of the natural world as it used to be. He always says hopeful things and is kind with players"; our Tom
  // Bombadil, named for the director's father, a painter). No beard, a bit tubby, glasses, sandals, and a different good hat
  // and waistcoat most nights: "extremely fashionable ... a true artist". He never says where he's from, why nothing touches
  // him, or how he breathes the air. He's merry, plain and kind, and he talks about the light.
  "dave": {
    "name": "Dave",
    "title": "a painter",
    "lines": [
      "Evening! Mind the wet paint. There. That's how the light lay on the hay at four o'clock. Do you remember it?",
      "They're out there, I know. Some nights they come and sit by me and watch me work. Never a cross word between us.",
      "You look tired, friend. The world's still lovely under all this. It's only resting.",
      "I paint what it was, so we'll know it when it comes back.",
      "Every morning's a morning somewhere. I've a feeling you'll see one.",
      "Where am I from? Oh, here and there. Mostly there. It was lovely there.",
      "Keep each other close. That's the whole trick of it. Always was.",
      "That's the bay in June. You can have it, if you can get it home dry.",
      "Don't hurry. The dark's in a hurry. You needn't be.",
      "The dark's not the opposite of light, you know. It's only light that hasn't got here yet.",
      "I did a sky on a wall in one of the forts, once. They seemed to like it. I hope they're keeping it clean.",
      "Hum something, if you like. No? Well. I'll hum for the both of us.",
      "Like the waistcoat? Found it in a trunk in a house nobody needed any more. It needed somebody.",
      "A fellow ought to have a good hat. The end of the world's no excuse for a bad one.",
      "Sandals, yes. My feet like to know where they are.",
      "Go on, then. They'll be wanting you on the train. I'll be about."
    ],
    // What he says to a blow, by how many times this one has struck him; at the last but one he sets his brush down and
    // turns to them (his telegraph). The last is his to say as he takes them by the neck.
    "blows": [
      "Easy, now. You'll muddy the sky.",
      "Ah. That's twice. We all have our bad nights, friend.",
      "Three times. I'd stop there, if I were you. I'm asking kindly.",
      "That's four. ... I've set my brush down. Think on it."
    ],
    "last": "You should be nicer in a dark world."
  }
}
